  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 39 actions (actions.js), registered in one setActionDefinitions call. The module defines no feedbacks (no setFeedbackDefinitions anywhere) and no variables; main.js only creates actions and presets. Presets (presets.js) are not catalogued because the schema has no preset field.",
    "Transport: UDP via UDPHelper to the configured Target IP and port (default '52381', main.js:119-125). sendCommand (main.js:69-81) sends Buffer.from(hex, 'hex') of the action string as is: the bytes are a plain VISCA command (8x ... FF) without the 8-byte VISCA-over-IP header (payload type, length, sequence number), although the instance keeps an unused sequenceNumber. Replies are only logged at debug level; the module reports status OK without checking the camera.",
    "All command bytes are fixed in the callbacks and use camera address 81. Dropdown ids are the hex nibbles the callback appends to the command and are strings; the catalog keeps them as written.",
    "focus_action: the choice ids '082' (Far (var)) and '083' (Near (var)) are three characters long as in the source. The callback appends Number(far).toString(16) (one hex digit for 0 to 15) to form the variable-speed command. The fixed choices '0802'/'0803' are the standard-speed Far/Near. The far and near number fields have min 0 and max 15 but no integer flag, a fractional value would produce a malformed command.",
    "preset_action, profile_action, multi_presenter_set_preset_action and auto_zoom_tilt_set_preset_action convert the number with Number(num).toString(16).padStart(2, '0'); the number fields declare min and max but no integer flag.",
    "frame_tracking_action, audio_tracking_action and auto_tracking_v1_action all send 8101047D<value>00FF; only the dropdown values differ. frame_tracking_action has default '02' (Auto Framing Mode) with choice ids '00', '02', '03'. video_mode_action has default '02' (NDI Only).",
    "pan_tilt_action: pan_speed and tilt_speed are both number fields with min 1 and max 24 (the labels say '1 (low) - 24 (high)'); they are hidden for Home ('04') and Reset ('05'), which send 810106<04|05>FF without speeds. The source isVisible uses a bitwise OR of two booleans; this works but is as written in the source.",
    "custom_action: a plain textinput without useVariables and without regex. All spaces are removed (replace(/ /g, '')) and the rest is passed to Buffer.from(..., 'hex'), which silently stops at the first invalid hex character; nothing validates the VISCA framing.",
    "Several actions share option ids across actions only by name (for example 'num'); every option id is unique inside its action. Choice ids are strings throughout, number fields are real numbers.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.12.1: options do not support expressions. Not tested against a camera or a running Companion instance; the catalog data comes from reading the source only."
  ]
}
